* Factorial by recursion: part 1 asks for part 1.
* JOSS has no arguments and no local values, so n is counted down on the
* way in and back up on the way out.
1.1 Set f = 1 if n ≤ 1.
1.2 Done if n ≤ 1.
1.3 Set n = n-1.
1.4 Do part 1.
1.5 Set n = n+1.
1.6 Set f = f·n.
Set n = 10.
Do part 1.
Type n, f.
